e-page-header-head-extra"><div><button style="margin-right:12px" class="suzume-btn suzume-btn-secondary suzume-btn-size-default suzume-btn-shape-square" type="button"><span>Cancel</span></button><button class="suzume-btn suzume-btn-primary suzume-btn-size-default suzume-btn-shape-square" type="button"><span>Save</span></button></div></div></div></div><div class="suzume-page-header-content"><div class="suzume-typography" style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:20px">For other uses, see Design</div><div class="suzume-typography">A design is a plan or specification for the construction of an object or system or for the implementation of an activity or process, or the result of that plan or specification in the form of a prototype, product or process. The verb to design expresses the process of developing a design. In some cases, the direct construction of an object without an explicit prior plan (such as in craftwork, some engineering, coding, and graphic design) may also be considered to be a design activity. The design usually has to satisfy certain goals and constraints, may take into account aesthetic, functional, economic, or socio-political considerations, and is expected to interact with a certain environment. Major examples of designs include architectural blueprints,engineering drawings, business processes, circuit diagrams, and sewing patterns.Major examples of designs include architectural blueprints,engineering drawings, business processes, circuit diagrams, and sewing patterns.</div></div></div></div>"`;
